=== citation_line_drift_check sairnsenior ===
  ANCHORED     : 0 -- the cited line names the resource, or reaches it in <=2 hops. This OUTRANKS distance: proximity to a write is a proxy, and on sd_comms the proxy inverted.
  SOUND        : 0 -- no direct reference, but within the window of a write site. The old rule, now a FALLBACK.
  DRIFTED      : 12
  INCONCLUSIVE : 6 -- no write site to point at, so NOT reported as drifted

DRIFTED means NOT ANCHORED TO A WRITE SITE. It does NOT mean the citation has moved, and the arrow is a CANDIDATE, not a correction to apply.
Before repointing any line above, read the register cell's own prose against the `cited line reads:` text. A cell may cite a render or field-construction site DELIBERATELY -- to prove a field is only rendered, or to show which fields are stored -- and this tool resolves write sites only, so it cannot tell those from a stale citation.
Measured both ways: sairnfreedom 32/32 were genuine drift (one uniform +825/+834 shift); sairngrounds 4/4 were deliberate read-site citations and repointing them would have broken four correct cells. Nothing here edits the document.
